cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TRACE: Trilinear Channel Estimation for Tri-Hybrid Architectures (MATLAB)"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the letter below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "de Almeida"
    given-names: "André L. F."
    email: "andre@gtel.ufc.br"
    affiliation: "Department of Teleinformatics Engineering, Federal University of Ceará, Fortaleza, Brazil"
  - family-names: "Liu"
    given-names: "Mengzhen"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/andrelimaferrer/TRACE-matlab"
abstract: >-
  Reference MATLAB implementation of TRACE, a trilinear (PARAFAC) channel
  estimator for the single-user uplink of a tri-hybrid receiver with
  pattern-reconfigurable antennas. Includes the ALS solver, the closed-form
  physical-parameter recovery stage, a greedy dictionary baseline, an
  oracle-support bound, and scripts reproducing every panel of the results
  figure. No third-party dependencies.
keywords:
  - channel estimation
  - tensor decomposition
  - PARAFAC
  - alternating least squares
  - reconfigurable antennas
  - tri-hybrid beamforming
  - MIMO

